lazysite (0.7.19-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * EDGE: SM156 - a domain configuration check. A Check button, a `domain-check`
    control-API action, and `lazysite-domains check <host>` report whether a
    registered domain resolves, points to this server, has a trusted HTTPS
    certificate, and terminates on THIS install (a new public CORS-open
    /.well-known/lazysite-instance.json marker). Server-side does the DNS/IP/TLS
    work a browser cannot; the panel adds a browser-side probe. The probe is
    bound to registered hosts (no SSRF) - which also tightened domain-preview.
  * EDGE: the preview gains an "Open live site" new-tab link beside its
    in-session render.
  * EDGE: domains preview fix - the page/domain preview shelled the wrapper's
    LAZYSITE_PROCESSOR, which the Apache/Hestia rewrite (and the dev server) set
    to the ORIGINALLY requested CGI - manager-api itself when a preview runs - so
    the preview re-entered manager-api with auth stripped and showed
    {"error":"Authentication required"}. Both previews now resolve
    lazysite-processor.pl by name in the cgi-bin.
  * EDGE: a domain alias mirrors its canonical's presentation (site title, theme,
    layout, nav, search), not just content_root + site_url; aliasing a sub-domain
    no longer shows the default site's title.
  * EDGE: the content folder is optional - a domain with none registers and
    serves the default site; reserved-path enforcement moves to a single
    Common::path_is_reserved / @RESERVED_ROOTS definition.
  * EDGE: a `domain` template variable (the sanitised host being served) lets one
    content folder render differently per domain.
  * EDGE: domains panel usability - full-width table-styled add form, auto-derived
    site address, friendly field labels + FQDN guidance, an overflow-safe curated
    table, and a styled inline edit row that pre-fills current values.
  * Hestia: lazysite-hestia-update-all.sh discovers by the Hestia web template
    (lazysite-hestia-list.sh --template-only), not the marker union, so a domain
    moved off the lazysite-app template is not updated; excluded marker-only
    domains are reported.

