lazysite (0.7.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First Debian packaging (SM139 increments 1+2): lazysite-common ships
    the engine payload at /usr/share/lazysite, the `lazysite` host CLI
    (provision / upgrade / upgrade --all / check / users / dev / version),
    the site registry directory /etc/lazysite/sites.d, generated man
    pages, and the lazysite@.service FastCGI pool template unit packaging
    the SM142 persistent runtime.
  * Provisioning model: no root writes into site trees - provision and
    upgrade run as the site user; only `upgrade --all` may run as root
    (drops to each site's owner per site).
  * New binary package lazysite-hestia (SM139 increment 4): HestiaCP
    integration as a hook-shaped command, superseding the hand-run
    installers/hestia scripts. Ships Apache web domain templates for
    both runtime patterns (lazysite-cgi: FallbackResource through the
    CGI auth wrapper; lazysite-fcgi: visitor pages proxied to the
    per-domain lazysite@ pool socket via mod_proxy_fcgi, auth/manager
    kept on the CGI path) under /usr/share/lazysite-hestia/templates,
    and /usr/bin/lazysite-hestia-domain (add/remove/list): root-run
    panel-side onboarding that prepares the locked Hestia domain root,
    drops to the panel user for provisioning, registers the site, and
    with --fcgi writes /etc/lazysite/pools/<domain>.conf and enables
    lazysite@<domain>.
  * lazysite-pool.pl now honours the SOCKET= pool-conf key it always
    documented (previously only --socket was read).

 -- Stuart J. Mackintosh <sjm@opendigital.cc>  Fri, 10 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0000
